or/projects/$HASH/agent-transcripts/*.jsonl\n```\n\n### 6. Round-trip proof — cursor resumes\n```\ncursor-agent --resume <agent-id-from-restored-dir>\n```\nSession should pick up prior context (foo.txt + prior turns visible).\n\n### 7. Resume path (separate from rewind)\n```\n/tmp/entire resume <branch>               # ExtraFiles dispatched via CheckpointRestorer\n```\nSame `~/.cursor/...` writes expected.\n\n## What each step proves\n\n| Step | Covers |\n|---|---|\n| 2 | `CheckpointContributor` (export) — already shipped, sanity |\n| 3→5 | `CheckpointRestorer.RestoreCheckpointFiles` via rewind |\n| 7 | `runCheckpointRestorer` via `RestoreLogsOnly` on resume |\n| 6 | End-to-end: Cursor actually reads restored `store.db` |\n\n## If something breaks\n\n- No archive in tree → export path. Check `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/checkpoint.go` (`ContributeCheckpointFiles`) fired — look in `.entire/logs/`.\n- Rewind skips cursor → `ExtraFiles` empty. Check `readExtraSessionFiles` in `checkpoint/committed.go`.\n- Files written but cursor ignores → workspace hash mismatch (cwd vs git root). `restore.go:52` uses cwd; ensure you ran from the same dir.\n\nUnit tests cover 2 + 5 deterministically; manual run above is for cursor-agent's own resume behavior."}],"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1271,"cache_read_input_tokens":77054,"output_tokens":1755,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1271,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":1755,"cache_read_input_tokens":77054,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1271,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1271},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaK7KDvuryynB8Kpiwz6G","type":"assistant","uuid":"9a468bcc-8422-4953-bc9e-3f6ee79b8cab","timestamp":