ge (grep found zero hits: /Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/cursor-export-import-sessions/cmd/entire/cli).\n- **Git blob deduplication works naturally** — identical bytes in `DBBytes` field would be deduplicated by git's content-addressable storage. However, **each Cursor DB changes every turn**, so each checkpoint's `DBBytes` blob is unique (no dedup across turns).\n- Archives are stored as **base64-encoded JSON** (chatexport.go:27-28), not compressed.\n\n## WAL/SHM Sidecar Storage\n\n**Code DOES ship WAL and SHM:**\n- `DBWALBytes` and `DBSHMBytes` fields in ChatArchive (chatexport.go:27-28)\n- Both read and base64-encoded at export time (lines 68-77)\n- Both restored on import (cursor/restore.go:79-80)\n\n**Size ratio from test seeds** (chatexport_test.go:82-85): Test uses 16 bytes for db + 17 bytes for WAL — not representative. Real data would show WAL >> DB, but code treats both equally. **No filtering/pruning of WAL sidecars.**\n\n## ExtraFiles Flow\n\n- Extracted at condensation (manual_commit_condensation.go:991): `extractExtraFilesFromTree` scans shadow tree for non-standard metadata files.\n- Passed through to committed checkpoint (line 253): `ExtraFiles: sessionData.ExtraFiles`\n- Written as blobs (committed.go:427-437): Each extra file becomes a git blob.\n- **Single path only** — no duplication. ExtraFiles written once to v1 branch.\n\n## Precedent for Pruning / External Storage\n\n**Only precedent found is `checkpoint_remote`:**\n- Configuration: CheckpointRemoteConfig (settings.go:687-690) — GitHub repo pointer.\n- **Not a general artifact store**, only routes the entire `entire/checkpoints/v1` branch to a separate repo (manual_commit_push.go:36).\n- **No precedent for:**\n  - Per-checkpoint artifact pruning\n  - Blob-level externalization (LFS, S3)\n  - WAL/SHM filtering\n  - Compression middleware\n\n**File location references:**\n- ContributeCheckpointFiles: cursor/checkpoint.go:17\n- WriteTemporary: temporary.go:114, 781-786\n- extractExtraFilesFromTree: