ne file per row, immutable per content hash\n```\n\n**Export**: open DB → `SELECT` rows → write files  \n**Import**: create empty DB → `CREATE TABLE` → `INSERT` rows back from files\n\nNeeds SQLite engine both sides. System `/usr/bin/sqlite3` on macOS (verified). Cursor users likely have it; gracefully fall back to shipping raw DB if absent.\n\n## Bonus benefits\n- Plain JSON in blobs → **redactor works correctly** (chat content IS sensitive; secrets should be redacted). Can revert the `isOpaqueAgentArchive` bypass from last push.\n- No WAL/SHM ever shipped — sqlite reads through them transparently when opening.\n- Human-readable archive for debugging.\n\nWriting plan now."}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2896,"cache_read_input_tokens":261797,"output_tokens":6538,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2896,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":6538,"cache_read_input_tokens":261797,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2896},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaNhYkgBbEXnhuAfGGBV9","type":"assistant","uuid":"fce9936f-ac12-437d-9f13-20bfb95fb70a","timestamp":"2026-04-24T13:48:01.567Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/cursor-export-import-sessions","sessionId":"4b7bf3d3-0d31-4237-918f-b56804225f2c","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"gtrrz-victor/cursor-export-import-sessions","slug":"great-i-did-see-swirling-honey"}
{"parentUuid":"fce9936f-ac12-437d-9f13-20bfb95fb70a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01Et5DSeaUZGdhrhw4RwfPc1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018afKain92Sb81rBEt1e4dr","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/.claude/plans/great-i-did-see-swirling-honey.md","content":"# Cursor archive v3 — row-level dump for git-native dedup\n\n## Context\n\nCurrent archive (v2, commit `c6e9c42d8`) ships the whole cursor `store.db`\nplus `store.db-wal` and `store.db-shm` as base64 blobs inside one JSON\nfile per checkpoint. Size per turn: ~340kB. The file lands on\n`entire/checkpoints/v1`, which is pushed to the remote on every\n`entire push`. Every turn adds a fresh ~340kB blob because base64-of-binary\ndefeats git's zlib packing and cursor's DB changes every turn, so git\nblob-level dedup doesn't fire either.\n\nInspection of a live cursor DB shows a very simple, content-addressable\nschema:\n\n```sql\nCREATE TABLE meta  (key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, value TEXT);   -- 1 row, hex-encoded JSON\nCREATE TABLE blobs (id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, data BLOB);     -- content-addressable Merkle DAG\n```\n\n`blobs.id` is the SHA256 of `blobs.data`. Each cursor \"save\" adds new\nblobs and updates `meta.latestRootBlobId`, but **old blobs are never\nmutated**. If we store each row as a separate git blob, git's native\ncontent-addressable storage deduplicates the unchanged rows across\ncheckpoints for free. Per-turn cost drops from ~340kB to ~few kB of\nnew blobs + a 500B `meta.json`.\n\nBonus: blobs are plain JSON (chat messages, tree nodes). They should\npass through the redactor — a previous fix in this PR had to add an\n`isOpaqueAgentArchive` bypass because base64-of-binary was matching\nfalse-positive secret patterns. With v3 that bypass becomes\nunnecessary and redaction does the right thing on real chat content.\n\n## Approach\n\nIntroduce `ChatArchive` version 3 with a directory layout:\n\n```\n.entire/metadata/<sessionID>/cursor-chat/\n  meta.json              # {\"agentId\": \"...\", \"latestRootBlobId\": \"...\", ...} — 500B\n  blobs/<blob-id>.json   # one file per blobs row (data is JSON text as found in DB)\n```\n\n`meta.json` holds the decoded JSON (current v2 stores it hex-encoded;\ndecoding costs nothing and makes the archive inspectable).\n`blobs/<id>.json` holds the exact bytes of `blobs.data` for that row.\n\n### Export (`ContributeCheckpointFiles` path)\n\n`cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go`:\n\n1. Locate `store.db` via the existing glob (`~/.cursor/chats/*/<agent-id>/store.db`).\n2. Copy `store.db`, `-wal`, `-shm` to a temp dir (cursor may hold them open).\n3. Open the temp copy with `sqlite3` CLI (shell out), `SELECT key, value FROM meta;` and `SELECT id, hex(data) FROM blobs;`.\n4. Write `meta.json` (hex-decode the `value` column to get plain JSON).\n5. Write `blobs/<id>.json` per row (hex-decode the `data` column).\n6. Delete temp copy.\n\nIf `sqlite3` is not on `PATH`, fall back to the current v2 behaviour\n(ship raw `store.db`+`-wal` base64) so we never block a checkpoint.\nLog a warn once per session.\n\n### Import (`RestoreCheckpointFiles` path)\n\n`cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go`:\n\n1. Detect archive version from `meta.json`'s sibling file, or by presence of `blobs/` dir (v3) vs old `.cursor-chat.json` (v2).\n2. For v3:\n   a. Create empty `store.db` at target path.\n   b. `sqlite3 <target> 'CREATE TABLE meta(...); CREATE TABLE blobs(...);'`.\n   c. For each `blobs/<id>.json`: `INSERT INTO blobs(id, data) VALUES(?, ?);` with the file bytes as BLOB.\n   d. `INSERT INTO meta(key, value)` with hex-encoded `meta.json` content, key `\"0\"`.\n   e. Do NOT write `store.db-wal` or `store.db-shm` — cursor will create them on next open.\n3. v2 path keeps existing restore logic for backwards compat during the transition (shadow branches and already-pushed checkpoints may still be v2).\n\n### Archive version detection\n\n`cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` defines `archiveVersion = 2` and the `ChatArchive` struct. For v3 we switch from \"one JSON file\" to \"a directory of files\". Use the presence of a `cursor-chat.meta.json` sentinel or `cursor-chat/` subdirectory under `.entire/metadata/<sid>/` to signal v3. Keep `ChatArchive` struct around for the v2 fallback path only.\n\n### SQLite CLI dependency\n\n`sqlite3` is nearly universal on macOS and mainstream Linux distros.\nBoth cursor and any cursor user already have SQLite installed\nsomewhere (cursor bundles it, our live test found `/usr/bin/sqlite3`).\nOn Windows it is less guaranteed; we fall back to v2.\n\nNo Go dep change. Binary size unchanged. Reverse of\n`c6e9c42d8`'s concern is avoided (it dropped an in-process sqlite\ndep; shelling out costs nothing at binary level).\n\n### Redactor\n\nRevert the `isOpaqueAgentArchive` bypass added in\n`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` (commit on this branch).\n`blobs/<id>.json` files are plain JSON with user messages and agent\noutput — exactly the content we want the redactor to sweep.\n`meta.json` is tiny boilerplate and gets redacted harmlessly.\n\n## Files to change\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` — add v3 export function; keep v2 for fallback.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go` — add v3 detection + restore; keep v2 path for legacy archives.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/checkpoint.go` — call the v3 exporter; v2 only if `sqlite3` absent.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` — revert `isOpaqueAgentArchive` bypass.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/extrafiles_test.go` — drop `TestCreateRedactedBlob_OpaqueArchive_NotRedacted` (no longer applicable); add a v3 roundtrip test.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport_test.go` — v3 export test.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/cursor_restore_test.go` — v3 restore assertion.\n\n## Reused functions and utilities\n\n- `cursor.WorkspaceHash`, `cursor.WorkspaceSlug` (restore.go) — already handle symlink-resolved cwd.\n- `checkpoint.extractExtraFilesFromTree` (condensation.go:1046) — already walks everything under the metadata dir; it picks up the `cursor-chat/` subtree automatically because `strings.HasPrefix(f.Name, metadataDir+\"/\")` matches anything deeper. Verify it does NOT skip subdirectories in a way that drops `blobs/*.json`. Current code at line 1060 has `if strings.Contains(relPath, \"/\") { return nil }` — **this skips subdirectories.** Needs a tweak to allow the `cursor-chat/` tree through. See verification section.\n- `checkpoint.readExtraSessionFiles` (committed.go:1039) — the symmetric reader. Same concern re subdirectories.\n- `ChunkJSONL` / `ReassembleJSONL` in `cmd/entire/cli/agent/agent.go` — not applicable to this data.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **No `sqlite3` on PATH**: fall back to v2 export. Log once. Restore still works for either format.\n- **DB in use (WAL frames pending)**: we copy DB+WAL+SHM to temp dir before opening. Opening via sqlite3 reads through WAL transparently, so we always get the consistent latest state.\n- **Empty session (no cursor-agent data yet)**: cursor doesn't have a DB yet. Exporter finds nothing and returns empty; checkpoint metadata just doesn't include a cursor-chat dir. Unchanged from today.\n- **Very large blobs**: git blob storage handles megabyte blobs fine; no limit concern.\n- **Concurrent cursor turns on same DB**: cursor serializes writes; our copy is a point-in-time snapshot. Future turns overwrite meta.json and add new blob files on next checkpoint.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Unit tests** (`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/ ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`):\n   - v3 export produces the expected directory layout from a seeded `store.db`.\n   - v3 restore rebuilds a DB whose `SELECT *` output matches the source.\n   - v2 archive still restores correctly (legacy path).\n   - Redactor test: confirm chat content containing secret-like strings gets redacted in the committed blob.\n\n2. **Size check**: add a test that runs 10 simulated turns (each adding 3 new blobs) and asserts the git pack size grows sub-linearly — i.e. new pack bytes per turn is roughly proportional to new blobs, not to total DB size.\n\n3. **Manual E2E** (existing script `/tmp/test-cursor-xfold.sh`):\n   - Folder A: one turn, commit → assert `.entire/metadata/<sid>/cursor-chat/` directory on the committed tree with `meta.json` + `blobs/*.json`.\n   - Assert base64 mega-blob no longer present.\n   - Folder B: `git clone`, `entire resume master` → assert store.db rebuilt with same row counts + same `meta.latestRootBlobId`.\n   - `cursor-agent --resume` in B → session picker shows session, selecting replays prior context.\n   - Run a second turn in B → new blobs appear; git pack grows only by the delta.\n\n4. **Condensation helper fix verification**: write an integration test that places a nested file (e.g. `.entire/metadata/<sid>/cursor-chat/blobs/foo.json`) on a shadow branch and asserts `extractExtraFilesFromTree` propagates it to the committed tree untouched.\n\n5. `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` all green before push.\n"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2896,"cache_read_input_tokens":261797,"output_tokens":6538,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2896,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":6538,"cache_read_input_tokens":261797,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2896,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2896},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaNhYkgBbEXnhuAfGGBV9","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6143935-ebfd-4300-ae71-6f4e7792f856","timestamp":"2026-04-24T13:48:58.204Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wk