{"parentUuid":"5f98c61b-6aff-489a-b96f-ddd50f7984d6","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-7","id":"msg_01XfhrBWC38CZzKdJyRC8jiJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CqhotHSK9a9WZsFwi4QCPk","name":"ExitPlanMode","input":{"allowedPrompts":[{"tool":"Bash","prompt":"run sqlite3 CLI on copies of cursor store.db to checkpoint WAL and read consolidated DB"},{"tool":"Bash","prompt":"run go build, go test, mise run fmt/lint/test:ci"},{"tool":"Bash","prompt":"run manual E2E script under /tmp to drive cursor-agent via tmux and verify archive size + restore fidelity"}],"plan":"# Cursor archive: shrink by WAL-checkpoint + gzip\n\n## Context\n\nCurrent archive (v2, commit `c6e9c42d8`) ships per checkpoint:\n\n```\nstore.db          (4–120 kB,  typically ~47 kB)\nstore.db-wal      (0–740 kB,  often the bulk of the archive)\nstore.db-shm      (0 or 32 kB, ephemeral index)\n```\n\nAll three base64-encoded into one JSON file per checkpoint on\n`entire/checkpoints/v1`. That branch is pushed to the remote on\nevery `entire push`, so per-turn archive size drives real network\nand pack-file cost.\n\nResearch findings:\n\n1. **DB itself is small.** Local sample of 15 sessions: min 4 kB,\n   max 119 kB, avg 47 kB. Largest (109 turns) gzips to 23 kB.\n   No pathological growth reports surfaced for the\n   `~/.cursor/chats/<md5>/<agent-id>/store.db` files.\n\n2. **Scary GB-scale cursor reports are for `state.vscdb`** (the\n   VS Code IDE workspace/global storage DB) — different file,\n   different path, not what we ship.\n\n3. **WAL is the primary bloat.** We observed WAL up to 740 kB on\n   a 4 kB DB — 185× the DB itself. WAL holds uncommitted\n   transactions; SQLite merges them into the main DB on next\n   open (`wal_checkpoint`). Cursor's next open would merge them,\n   but ship-side we still pay the WAL bytes in git.\n\n4. **Schema is 2 tables.** `meta(key TEXT, value TEXT)` holds a\n   500-byte hex-encoded JSON root pointer. `blobs(id TEXT, data\n   BLOB)` holds a content-addressable Merkle DAG of chat messages\n   and tree nodes. All immutable per content hash.\n\nConclusion: a full row-level git-native dedup layout (my first\ndraft of this plan) is over-engineering for sub-100 kB files. The\n90% win comes from **checkpointing the WAL before archiving and\ndropping the WAL/SHM sidecars from the archive**. Add gzip for\nanother ~50% on top.\n\n## Approach\n\nBump to archive v3. Shape unchanged (still one `<sid>.cursor-chat.json`\nfile per checkpoint), content tightened:\n\n```json\n{\n  \"format\":  \"cursor-chat-export\",\n  \"version\": 3,\n  \"agentId\": \"...\",\n  \"db_gzip_b64\": \"<gzip(store.db) base64>\"\n}\n```\n\nRemoved: `db_bytes`, `db_wal_bytes`, `db_shm_bytes`, `db_path`,\n`transcript`, `transcript_path`. (Transcript already lives as\n`.entire/metadata/<sid>/full.jsonl`; shipping it again inside the\narchive was redundant.)\n\n### Export (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go`)\n\n1. Find `store.db` (existing glob).\n2. Copy `store.db`, `-wal`, `-shm` to a temp dir (cursor may hold them open).\n3. If `sqlite3` CLI is on PATH: `sqlite3 <temp>/store.db 'PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE); VACUUM;'` — consolidates WAL into DB, truncates WAL to 0, reclaims free pages.\n4. Read consolidated `store.db` bytes, gzip, base64-encode, pack into v3 archive.\n5. If `sqlite3` not on PATH: **fall back to v2 format** (current behavior). Log a warn once per session.\n6. Delete temp dir.\n\n### Restore (`cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go`)\n\n1. Detect version from `archive.Version`.\n2. v3: base64-decode → gunzip → write `store.db` at target. Do NOT write `-wal` or `-shm` (cursor creates them fresh on next open).\n3. v2: keep existing code path for backward compat with already-pushed checkpoints.\n4. Both paths continue using `WorkspaceHash` (md5 of symlink-resolved cwd) and write to `~/.cursor/chats/<hash>/<agent-id>/store.db`.\n5. Transcript path (projects/<slug>/agent-transcripts/<id>/<id>.jsonl) is handled separately by the main transcript flow — unchanged.\n\n### Redactor\n\nBecause the v3 archive still wraps binary (now gzipped DB) as base64\ninside JSON, the redactor still needs the bypass we added last push\n(`isOpaqueAgentArchive`). Keep it.\n\n### No SQLite dep added to the Go binary\n\nShell out to the system `sqlite3` CLI. Verified present at\n`/usr/bin/sqlite3` on this Mac. Nearly universal on mainstream\nmacOS and Linux; Cursor itself doesn't install it but most dev\nenvironments already have it. Windows: less predictable → falls\nback to v2 gracefully.\n\nIf we later want a hard guarantee across platforms without\nshipping a 5.5 MB dep, revisit `modernc.org/sqlite`.\n\n## Expected size impact\n\n| archive | typical bytes | long session bytes |\n|---|---|---|\n| current v2 (db + wal + shm, base64-in-JSON) | 340 000 | 1 000 000+ |\n| v3 (db only, gzip, base64-in-JSON) | 15 000 – 25 000 | 50 000 |\n| reduction | ~15× | ~20× |\n\n## Files to change\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` — new v3 writer; keep v2 writer for fallback; new `ChatArchive.DBGzipBase64` field.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go` — branch on version; v3 reads `DBGzipBase64`, gunzips, writes only `store.db`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport_test.go` — roundtrip test for v3; keep v2 tests.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/cursor_restore_test.go` — v3 archive round-trip assertion.\n\n## Reused utilities\n\n- `cursor.WorkspaceHash`, `cursor.WorkspaceSlug` in restore.go — unchanged.\n- `os/exec` for sqlite3 shell-out; no new Go dependencies.\n- `compress/gzip`, `encoding/base64`, `encoding/json` — all stdlib.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **No `sqlite3` on PATH**: fall back to v2 format. User keeps working with the bloated-but-correct archive. We log a one-time warning.\n- **Cursor holds DB open**: copy DB+WAL+SHM to temp dir before checkpointing. Avoids touching cursor's live files.\n- **Empty session (no DB yet)**: nothing to export. Archive just not included, same as today.\n- **v2 archive already in remote history**: restore detects version, uses v2 path. No migration needed.\n- **Path containing special chars**: `WorkspaceSlug` currently does a naive slash-to-dash replace but cursor uses a regex that also strips non-alphanumerics. Keep the existing two-pronged glob in export to handle both; no change in this PR.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Unit**: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/ ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` covers:\n   - v3 export on a seeded DB (with active WAL) produces a small gzip blob and the DB-after-restore equals the DB-after-checkpoint-on-source.\n   - v2 archive still restores correctly.\n   - No-sqlite3 path: rename PATH temporarily, verify fallback to v2.\n\n2. **Size check**: in the roundtrip test, assert `len(v3 archive) < len(v2 archive) / 5` for any seeded DB ≥ 20 kB with non-empty WAL.\n\n3. **Manual E2E**: `/tmp/test-cursor-xfold.sh` (already exists) with two extra assertions:\n   - `git cat-file -s <archive-blob>` on `entire/checkpoints/v1` for the committed checkpoint is in the single-digit-kB range (well under 50 kB).\n   - After 5 sequential turns, git pack size grows roughly linearly with new DB content only.\n\n4. `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` green.\n\n## Appendix — `~/.cursor/` inventory (session-relevant only)\n\nFull inventory investigated. Of everything under `~/.cursor/`, only two paths are per-session and need archiving:\n\n- `chats/<md5>/<agent-id>/store.db[-wal|-shm]` — cursor's chat DAG. We archive the `store.db` content only.\n- `projects/<slug>/agent-transcripts/<agent-id>/<agent-id>.jsonl` — JSONL turn log. Already shipped.\n\nSkipped because not session-specific or not load-bearing:\n- `projects/<slug>/repo.json` — cursor's per-cwd UUID; cross-folder test confirmed resume works with different UUIDs on each end.\n- `projects/<slug>/.workspace-trusted` — trust dialog. Security: let user re-confirm in a new cwd.\n- `projects/<slug>/worker.log`, `worker.sock` — LSP logs and IPC.\n- Global config, caches, telemetry, extensions (~450 MB of binaries).\n\n## Option held in reserve — row-level layout\n\nIf DBs turn out to grow beyond ~500 kB in real usage, or if we want cross-checkpoint git blob dedup, switch to v4 with a directory layout: `cursor-chat/meta.json` plus `cursor-chat/blobs/<id>.json` per row (content-addressable, git-native dedup). Deferred — current evidence doesn't justify the complexity.\n","planFilePath":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/.claude/plans/great-i-did-see-swirling-honey.md"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6638,"cache_read_input_tokens":289033,"output_tokens":227,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6638,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"","iterations":[{"input_tokens":1,"output_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":289033,"cache_creation_input_tokens":6638,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":6638},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"}},"requestId":"req_011CaNiKti8ownchzszp15QW","type":"assistant","uuid":"1bd015c5-8b7a-41bd-8fc9-773b1c4b9428","timestamp":"2026-04-24T13:57:38.233Z","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/gtrrz-victor/wks/cli/cursor-export-import-sessions","sessionId":"4b7bf3d3-0d31-4237-918f-b56804225f2c","version":"2.1.117","gitBranch":"gtrrz-victor/cursor-export-import-sessions","slug":"great-i-did-see-swirling-honey"}
