, one per line\n  full.jsonl          # existing: transcript, unchanged\n  prompt.txt          # existing\n```\n\n### `cursor-chat.jsonl` format\n\nOne JSON object per line. Line order: meta first, then blobs in\nstable order (sort by `id` ascending for determinism — helps git\npack delta compression across checkpoints).\n\n```jsonl\n{\"t\":\"meta\",\"k\":\"0\",\"v\":{\"agentId\":\"...\",\"latestRootBlobId\":\"...\",\"name\":\"File Creator\",\"mode\":\"default\",\"createdAt\":1772413408645,\"lastUsedModel\":\"default\"}}\n{\"t\":\"blob\",\"id\":\"<sha256>\",\"data\":\"<base64(raw bytes)>\"}\n{\"t\":\"blob\",\"id\":\"<sha256>\",\"data\":\"<base64(raw bytes)>\"}\n...\n```\n\nFields:\n- `t`: row type, `\"meta\"` or `\"blob\"`.\n- Meta line: `k` = `meta.key`; `v` = **decoded** JSON object (source is hex-encoded in DB; we decode for plain-text ship).\n- Blob line: `id` = `blobs.id`; `data` = base64 of `blobs.data`.\n\nOther v2 archive fields are dropped (`db_bytes`, `db_wal_bytes`,\n`db_shm_bytes`, `db_path`, `transcript`, `transcript_path`) — WAL/SHM\nbytes no longer shipped; transcript already lives at `full.jsonl`.\n\n### Export — `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go`\n\n1. Locate live `store.db` (existing glob).\n2. Copy `store.db`, `-wal`, `-shm` to temp dir (cursor may hold them open).\n3. `sqlite3 temp/store.db 'PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE); VACUUM;'` — absorbs WAL into DB, reclaims free pages.\n4. `sqlite3 temp/store.db -separator '|' 'SELECT key, value FROM meta;'` → build meta line.\n5. `sqlite3 temp/store.db 'SELECT id, hex(data) FROM blobs ORDER BY id;'` → build blob lines.\n6. Write `cursor-chat.jsonl` to the session metadata dir.\n7. Delete temp dir.\n\nIf `sqlite3` not on PATH: log a one-time warn, fall back to the existing v2 writer (ships raw bytes base64). Always succeeds; backward-compatible.\n\n### Import — `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go`\n\n1. Detect version:\n   - If `cursor-chat.jsonl` present in `files` map → v3.\n   - Else if `<sid>.cursor-chat.json` present → v2 (fall through to existing code).\n2. v3 path:\n   a. Resolve target `store.db` path: `~/.cursor/chats/<md5(resolved cwd)>/<agent-id>/store.db`. Reuse existing `WorkspaceHash` + `EvalSymlinks` logic.\n   b. `mkdir -p` parent.\n   c. Pipe `CREATE TABLE meta(key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, value TEXT); CREATE TABLE blobs(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, data BLOB);` into `sqlite3 target/store.db`.\n   d. For each JSONL line:\n      - `meta`: emit `INSERT INTO meta (key, value) VALUES ('0', hex);` where `hex` = hex encoding of JSON-marshaled `v`. Pipe to sqlite3 in a batch.\n      - `blob`: emit `INSERT INTO blobs (id, data) VALUES ('<id>', x'<hex(base64-decode(data))>');`. Pipe to sqlite3.\n   e. Do NOT write `-wal` or `-shm` — cursor creates them fresh on next open.\n3. Everything else (transcript writing, WorkspaceSlug nested-path layout, symlink resolution) unchanged.\n\n### Redactor\n\nRevert the `isOpaqueAgentArchive` bypass for `.cursor-chat.json` (old v2\nextension) **but extend it to the new `.cursor-chat.jsonl`**. Reason:\nblob rows still carry base64 payloads on individual lines. The JSONL\nredactor is line-oriented and could match a secret pattern *inside*\nthe base64 `data` field, corrupting one row. One-liner in\n`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go:isOpaqueAgentArchive`:\n\n```go\nreturn strings.HasSuffix(treePath, \".cursor-chat.jsonl\") ||\n       strings.HasSuffix(treePath, \".cursor-chat.json\")\n```\n\n(Keep v2 suffix for already-pushed archives on the remote.)\n\n### SQLite requirement\n\nShell out to the system `sqlite3` CLI. Verified present at\n`/usr/bin/sqlite3` on this Mac. Ubiquitous on mainstream Linux; macOS\nships it. Windows unreliable → falls back to v2 gracefully.\n\nNo Go dep change. Binary size unchanged.\n\n## Expected size impact\n\n| archive | raw bytes | git pack bytes | ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| v2 (current) | ~340 kB | ~300 kB | 1× |\n| v3 JSONL (typical) | 20–30 kB | 7–10 kB | **30–40× smaller** |\n| v3 JSONL (109-turn session) | ~90 kB | ~25 kB | **~12× smaller** |\n\n## Files to change\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` — add v3 JSONL writer; keep v2 writer for fallback when sqlite3 absent. Bump `archiveVersion = 3`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go` — add v3 detection + JSONL restorer; keep v2 path.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/checkpoint.go` — `ContributeCheckpointFiles` calls the v3 path when available.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` — extend `isOpaqueAgentArchive` to include `.cursor-chat.jsonl`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport_test.go` — v3 roundtrip test (seed a DB with meta + N blobs, export, parse JSONL, assert rows match).\n- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/cursor_restore_test.go` — v3 restore test; open reconstructed DB via sqlite3 and assert `SELECT` returns the same rows.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/extrafiles_test.go` — keep `TestCreateRedactedBlob_OpaqueArchive_NotRedacted`; add a case asserting `.cursor-chat.jsonl` also bypasses.\n\n## Reused utilities\n\n- `cursor.WorkspaceHash`, `cursor.WorkspaceSlug` (restore.go) — unchanged.\n- `os/exec` for sqlite3 shell-out — no new dependencies.\n- `encoding/json`, `encoding/base64`, `encoding/hex` — stdlib.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- **No `sqlite3` on PATH**: fall back to v2 writer. One-time log warn.\n- **Cursor holds DB open**: copy DB+WAL+SHM to temp dir before opening.\n- **Empty session**: no DB found, archive file absent. Same as today.\n- **v2 archive already pushed to remote**: restore detects via `.cursor-chat.json` presence, uses v2 path. No migration.\n- **Path containing special chars**: no change from current handling.\n- **Very large `data` blob**: sqlite has no practical row size limit for our inputs. Base64 in JSONL is fine.\n- **Malformed JSONL line** during restore: skip, log warn, continue. Better than aborting restore for a single-row corruption.\n\n## Verification\n\n1. **Unit tests** (`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/ ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`):\n   - v3 export: seed DB with `meta` + 20 blobs, call exporter, parse JSONL, assert line count = 21 and each row present.\n   - v3 restore: feed JSONL to restorer, open resulting `store.db` with sqlite3, assert `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM blobs` and `SELECT value FROM meta` equal the source.\n   - v2 archive still restores correctly (backward compat).\n   - No-sqlite3: mask PATH, verify exporter falls back to v2 and doesn't error.\n   - Redactor: assert a `.cursor-chat.jsonl` with a secret-looking token in a blob's base64 payload survives the redaction pass byte-for-byte.\n\n2. **Size check in test**: assert v3 archive bytes < 1/5 of v2 archive bytes for the same seeded DB.\n\n3. **Manual E2E** (existing `/tmp/test-cursor-xfold.sh`):\n   - Folder A → commit → assert `cursor-chat.jsonl` on `entire/checkpoints/v1` tree.\n   - `git cat-file -s` on the archive blob is single-digit kB.\n   - Folder B `entire resume master` → `store.db` rebuilt with matching row counts + `meta.latestRootBlobId`.\n   - `cursor-agent --resume` in B → session picker shows restored session; selecting it loads prior context.\n   - Follow-up turn in B → cursor writes new rows; next commit ships only the delta lines.\n\n4. `mise run fmt && mise run lint && mise run test:ci` green.\n\n## Appendix — `~/.cursor/` inventory (session-relevant only)\n\n- `chats/<md5>/<agent-id>/store.db[-wal|-shm]` — cursor's chat DAG. v3 archives rows only.\n- `projects/<slug>/agent-transcripts/<agent-id>/<agent-id>.jsonl` — turn log. Already shipped.\n\nEverything else under `~/.cursor/` (450MB extensions, global config, IDE state, trust flags, worker logs) is either global, per-cwd-at-cursor's-choice, or ephemeral — skip.\n\n## Option held in reserve — row-per-file directory layout\n\nIf we ever want cross-checkpoint git blob dedup (git dedupes whole blobs, not lines within a blob), switch to a `cursor-chat/meta.json` + `cursor-chat/blobs/<id>.bin` directory layout. Deferred — JSONL is simpler and already gets us a ~30× reduction.\n","structuredPatch":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":158,"newStart":1,"newLines":177,"lines":["-# Cursor archive: shrink by WAL-checkpoint + gzip","+# Cursor archive v3: JSONL row dump"," "," ## Context"," "," Current archive (v2, commit `c6e9c42d8`) ships per checkpoint:"," "," ```","-store.db          (4–120 kB,  typically ~47 kB)","-store.db-wal      (0–740 kB,  often the bulk of the archive)","-store.db-shm      (0 or 32 kB, ephemeral index)","+store.db          (4–120 kB, typically ~47 kB)","+store.db-wal      (0–740 kB, often the bulk)","+store.db-shm      (0 or 32 kB)"," ```"," "," All three base64-encoded into one JSON file per checkpoint on","-`entire/checkpoints/v1`. That branch is pushed to the remote on","-every `entire push`, so per-turn archive size drives real network","-and pack-file cost.","+`entire/checkpoints/v1`. That branch pushes to the remote on every","+`entire push`, so per-turn archive size drives real network and","+pack-file cost."," ","-Research findings:","+Research:"," ","-1. **DB itself is small.** Local sample of 15 sessions: min 4 kB,","-   max 119 kB, avg 47 kB. Largest (109 turns) gzips to 23 kB.","-   No pathological growth reports surfaced for the","-   `~/.cursor/chats/<md5>/<agent-id>/store.db` files.","+- **DB is small** (15 local sessions: min 4 kB, max 119 kB, avg 47 kB).","+- **WAL is the bulk.** We observed WAL up to 740 kB on a 4 kB DB — 185× the DB.","+- **Schema is 2 tables.** `meta(key, value)` holds a 500-byte hex-encoded JSON root pointer. `blobs(id, data)` is a content-addressable Merkle DAG of chat messages and tree nodes. All immutable per content hash.","+- **Scary GB-scale cursor reports** (7 GB, 11 GB) target `state.vscdb`, VS Code IDE storage — different file, not what we ship."," ","-2. **Scary GB-scale cursor reports are for `state.vscdb`** (the","-   VS Code IDE workspace/global storage DB) — different file,","-   different path, not what we ship.","+Conclusion: a JSO