"," ","-- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` — new v3 writer; keep v2 writer for fallback; new `ChatArchive.DBGzipBase64` field.","-- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go` — branch on version; v3 reads `DBGzipBase64`, gunzips, writes only `store.db`.","-- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport_test.go` — roundtrip test for v3; keep v2 tests.","-- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/cursor_restore_test.go` — v3 archive round-trip assertion.","+- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` — add v3 JSONL writer; keep v2 writer for fallback when sqlite3 absent. Bump `archiveVersion = 3`.","+- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go` — add v3 detection + JSONL restorer; keep v2 path.","+- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/checkpoint.go` — `ContributeCheckpointFiles` calls the v3 path when available.","+- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go` — extend `isOpaqueAgentArchive` to include `.cursor-chat.jsonl`.","+- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport_test.go` — v3 roundtrip test (seed a DB with meta + N blobs, export, parse JSONL, assert rows match).","+- `cmd/entire/cli/strategy/cursor_restore_test.go` — v3 restore test; open reconstructed DB via sqlite3 and assert `SELECT` returns the same rows.","+- `cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/extrafiles_test.go` — keep `TestCreateRedactedBlob_OpaqueArchive_NotRedacted`; add a case asserting `.cursor-chat.jsonl` also bypasses."," "," ## Reused utilities"," ","-- `cursor.WorkspaceHash`, `cursor.WorkspaceSlug` in restore.go — unchanged.","-- `os/exec` for sqlite3 shell-out; no new Go dependencies.","-- `compress/gzip`, `encoding/base64`, `encoding/json` — all stdlib.","+- `cursor.WorkspaceHash`, `cursor.WorkspaceSlug` (restore.go) — unchanged.","+- `os/exec` for sqlite3 shell-out — no new dependencies.","+- `encoding/json`, `encoding/base64`, `encoding/hex` — stdlib."," "," ## Edge cases"," ","-- **No `sqlite3` on PATH**: fall back to v2 format. User keeps working with the bloated-but-correct archive. We log a one-time warning.","-- **Cursor holds DB open**: copy DB+WAL+SHM to temp dir before checkpointing. Avoids touching cursor's live files.","-- **Empty session (no DB yet)**: nothing to export. Archive just not included, same as today.","-- **v2 archive already in remote history**: restore detects version, uses v2 path. No migration needed.","-- **Path containing special chars**: `WorkspaceSlug` currently does a naive slash-to-dash replace but cursor uses a regex that also strips non-alphanumerics. Keep the existing two-pronged glob in export to handle both; no change in this PR.","+- **No `sqlite3` on PATH**: fall back to v2 writer. One-time log warn.","+- **Cursor holds DB open**: copy DB+WAL+SHM to temp dir before opening.","+- **Empty session**: no DB found, archive file absent. Same as today.","+- **v2 archive already pushed to remote**: restore detects via `.cursor-chat.json` presence, uses v2 path. No migration.","+- **Path containing special chars**: no change from current handling.","+- **Very large `data` blob**: sqlite has no practical row size limit for our inputs. Base64 in JSONL is fine.","+- **Malformed JSONL line** during restore: skip, log warn, continue. Better than aborting restore for a single-row corruption."," "," ## Verification"," ","-1. **Unit**: `go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/ ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/` covers:","-   - v3 export on a seeded DB (with active WAL) produces a small gzip blob and the DB-after-restore equals the DB-after-checkpoint-on-source.","-   - v2 archive still restores correctly.","-   - No-sqlite3 path: rename PATH temporarily, verify fallback to v2.","+1. **Unit tests** (`go test ./cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/ ./cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/ ./cmd/entire/cli/strategy/`):","+   - v3 export: seed DB with `meta` + 20 blobs, call exporter, parse JSONL, assert line count = 21 and each row present.","+   - v3 restore: feed JSONL to restorer, open resulting `store.db` with sqlite3, assert `SELECT COUNT(*) FROM blobs` and `SELECT value FROM meta` equal