ELECT id, data FROM blobs ORDER BY id` → base64-encode `data`, emit one line per row.\n6. Write `cursor-chat.jsonl` to the session metadata dir.\n7. Close DB, delete temp dir.\n\nNo fallback code path — modernc.org/sqlite is in the binary, works on every platform we ship to (including Windows without CGo).","originalFile":"# Cursor archive v3: JSONL row dump\n\n## Context\n\nCurrent archive (v2, commit `c6e9c42d8`) ships per checkpoint:\n\n```\nstore.db          (4–120 kB, typically ~47 kB)\nstore.db-wal      (0–740 kB, often the bulk)\nstore.db-shm      (0 or 32 kB)\n```\n\nAll three base64-encoded into one JSON file per checkpoint on\n`entire/checkpoints/v1`. That branch pushes to the remote on every\n`entire push`, so per-turn archive size drives real network and\npack-file cost.\n\nResearch:\n\n- **DB is small** (15 local sessions: min 4 kB, max 119 kB, avg 47 kB).\n- **WAL is the bulk.** We observed WAL up to 740 kB on a 4 kB DB — 185× the DB.\n- **Schema is 2 tables.** `meta(key, value)` holds a 500-byte hex-encoded JSON root pointer. `blobs(id, data)` is a content-addressable Merkle DAG of chat messages and tree nodes. All immutable per content hash.\n- **Scary GB-scale cursor reports** (7 GB, 11 GB) target `state.vscdb`, VS Code IDE storage — different file, not what we ship.\n\nConclusion: a JSONL row-dump of the two tables, plus WAL checkpoint\nbefore export, gives 30-50× smaller archives than today, with plain-\ntext contents that git packs very well.\n\n## Approach\n\nIntroduce archive v3. Ship one new file alongside the existing\ntranscript, not a monolithic JSON blob:\n\n```\n.entire/metadata/<sessionID>/\n  cursor-chat.jsonl   # new: DB rows, one per line\n  full.jsonl          # existing: transcript, unchanged\n  prompt.txt          # existing\n```\n\n### `cursor-chat.jsonl` format\n\nOne JSON object per line. Line order: meta first, then blobs in\nstable order (sort by `id` ascending for determinism — helps git\npack delta compression across checkpoints).\n\n```jsonl\n{\"t\":\"meta\",\"k\":\"0\",\"v\":{\"agentId\":\"...\",\"latestRootBlobId\":\"...\",\"name\":\"File Creator\",\"mode\":\"default\",\"createdAt\":1772413408645,\"lastUsedModel\":\"default\"}}\n{\"t\":\"blob\",\"id\":\"<sha256>\",\"data\":\"<base64(raw bytes)>\"}\n{\"t\":\"blob\",\"id\":\"<sha256>\",\"data\":\"<base64(raw bytes)>\"}\n...\n```\n\nFields:\n- `t`: row type, `\"meta\"` or `\"blob\"`.\n- Meta line: `k` = `meta.key`; `v` = **decoded** JSON object (source is hex-encoded in DB; we decode for plain-text ship).\n- Blob line: `id` = `blobs.id`; `data` = base64 of `blobs.data`.\n\nOther v2 archive fields are dropped (`db_bytes`, `db_wal_bytes`,\n`db_shm_bytes`, `db_path`, `transcript`, `transcript_path`) — WAL/SHM\nbytes no longer shipped; transcript already lives at `full.jsonl`.\n\n### Export — `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go`\n\n1. Locate live `store.db` (existing glob).\n2. Copy `store.db`, `-wal`, `-shm` to temp dir (cursor may hold them open).\n3. `sqlite3 temp/store.db 'PRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE); VACUUM;'` — absorbs WAL into DB, reclaims free pages.\n4. `sqlite3 temp/store.db -separator '|' 'SELECT key, value FROM meta;'` → build meta line.\n5. `sqlite3 temp/store.db 'SELECT id, hex(data) FROM blobs ORDER BY id;'` → build blob lines.\n6. Write `cursor-chat.jsonl` to the session metadata dir.\n7. Delete temp dir.\n\nIf `sqlite3` not on PATH: log a one-time warn, fall back to the existing v2 writer (ships raw bytes base64). Always succeeds; backward-compatible.\n\n### Import — `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go`\n\n1. Detect version:\n   - If `cursor-chat.jsonl` present in `files` map → v3.\n   - Else if `<sid>.cursor-chat.json` present → v2 (fall through to existing code).\n2. v3 path:\n   a. Resolve target `store.db` path: `~/.cursor/chats/<md5(resolved cwd)>/<agent-id>/store.db`. Reuse existing `WorkspaceHash` + `EvalSymlinks` logic.\n   b. `mkdir -p` parent.\n   c. Pipe `CREATE TABLE meta(key TEXT PRIMARY KEY, value TEXT); CREATE TABLE blobs(id TEXT PRIMARY KEY, data BLOB);` into `sqlite3 target/store.db`.\n   d. For each JSONL line:\n      - `meta`: emit `INSERT INTO meta (key, value) VALUES ('0', hex);` where `hex` = hex encoding of JSON-marshaled `v`. Pipe to sqlite3 in a batch.\n      - `blob`: emit `INSERT INTO blobs (id, data) VALUES ('<id>', x'<hex(base64-decode(data))>');`. Pipe to sqlite3.\n   e. Do NOT write `-wal` or `-shm` — cursor creates them fresh on next open.\n3. Everything else (transcript writing, WorkspaceSlug nested-path layout, symlink resolution) unchanged.\n\n### Redactor\n\nRevert the `isOpaqueAgentArchive` bypass for `.cursor-chat.json` (old v2\nextension) **but extend it to the new `.cursor-chat.jsonl`**. Reason:\nblob rows still carry base64 payloads on individual lines. The JSONL\nredactor is line-oriented and could match a secret pattern *inside*\nthe base64 `data` field, corrupting one row. One-liner in\n`cmd/entire/cli/checkpoint/committed.go:isOpaqueAgentArchive`:\n\n```go\nreturn strings.HasSuffix(treePath, \".cursor-chat.jsonl\") ||\n       strings.HasSuffix(treePath, \".cursor-chat.json\")\n```\n\n(Keep v2 suffix for already-pushed archives on the remote.)\n\n### SQLite requirement\n\nShell out to the system `sqlite3` CLI. Verified present at\n`/usr/bin/sqlite3` on this Mac. Ubiquitous on mainstream Linux; macOS\nships it. Windows unreliable → falls back to v2 gracefully.\n\nNo Go dep change. Binary size unchanged.\n\n## Expected size impact\n\n| archive | raw bytes | git pack bytes | ratio |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| v2 (current) | ~340 kB | ~300 kB | 1× |\n| v3 JSONL (typical) | 20–30 kB | 7–10 kB | **30–40× smaller** |\n| v3 JSONL (109-turn session) | ~90 kB | ~25 kB | **~12× smaller** |\n\n## Files to change\n\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/chatexport.go` — add v3 JSONL writer; keep v2 writer for fallback when sqlite3 absent. Bump `archiveVersion = 3`.\n- `cmd/entire/cli/agent/cursor/restore.go` — add v3 detection + JSONL restorer; keep 